# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Albert Ray's Repairs & Restoration — notification settings
#
# The site works WITHOUT any of these set: new bookings and
# contact messages are logged to the server console. Fill these
# in to turn on real email + SMS notifications. No code changes
# are needed — the app detects the keys at runtime.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Email (Resend) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign up at https://resend.com, create an API key.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Verified sender. Until you verify your own domain you can use
# the Resend sandbox: "Albert Ray's Repairs & Restoration <onboarding@resend.dev>"
RESEND_FROM=
# Where lead notifications are delivered (Albert's inbox).
NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# Optional: replies to notification emails go here.
NOTIFY_REPLY_TO=

# ── SMS (Twilio) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# From https://console.twilio.com
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# A Twilio phone number you own, e.g. +15125550123
TWILIO_FROM=
# Where lead texts are delivered (Albert's cell), e.g. +15125550199
NOTIFY_PHONE=

# ── Database (Neon Postgres) ────────────────────────────────
# Optional today: when unset, leads are NOT persisted (the app
# logs and keeps working). Set this to turn on the lead database
# and the admin CRM — no code changes needed.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a free project at https://neon.tech
#   2. Copy the "Pooled connection" string from the dashboard
#      (Connection Details → Connection string).
#   3. Paste it below, then run:  npm run db:migrate
#
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DBNAME?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Admin / Ops console (/admin) ────────────────────────────
# Optional today: when unset, /admin shows a setup notice and is
# NOT protected. Set BOTH to lock the console and enable sign-in.
#
# ADMIN_PASSWORD — the single password Albert types to sign in.
# AUTH_SECRET    — random key that signs the session cookie.
#                  Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Payments / Stripe (card payments on quotes) ─────────────
# Optional today: when unset, manual cash/check payments still
# work and the "Payment link" button returns a friendly 503.
# Card payments use Stripe HOSTED Checkout — no card data ever
# touches this app.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create an account at https://stripe.com
#   2. STRIPE_SECRET_KEY  — Developers → API keys → Secret key (sk_live_… / sk_test_…)
#   3. STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET — Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint
#      https://YOUR_DOMAIN/api/stripe/webhook (event: checkout.session.completed),
#      then copy its "Signing secret" (whsec_…). For local testing:
#      stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook
#   4. NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL — your site origin, used for success/cancel URLs.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
